        "original_id": "58f76cab-34ec-5a22-8700-ad510d531e84",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincent Cirelli, Ridley Scott, Jon Spaihts, Damon Lindelof, Noomi Rapace, Michael Fassbender, Guy Pearce, Idris Elba, Logan Marshall-Green, Charlize Theron\n- Companies: Luma Pictures\n- Films: Prometheus, No Country for Old Men, The Midnight Meat Train, Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince, The Book of Eli, The Avengers, Saving Mr. Banks, Guardians of the Galaxy, In the Heart of the Sea, Deadpool, Doctor Strange\n- Roles: visual effects supervisor, director, writer, actor\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Visual Effects, 89th Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 2007, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on No Country for Old Men.\n- In 2008, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on The Midnight Meat Train.\n- In 2009, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince.\n- In 2010, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on The Book of Eli.\n- In 2012, Prometheus was released as a science fiction film directed by Ridley Scott and written by Jon Spaihts and Damon Lindelof.\n- In 2012, Prometheus starred Noomi Rapace, Michael Fassbender, Guy Pearce, Idris Elba, Logan Marshall-Green, and Charlize Theron.\n- In 2012, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on Prometheus and The Avengers.\n- In 2013, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on Saving Mr. Banks.\n- In 2014, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on Guardians of the Galaxy.\n- In 2015, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on In the Heart of the Sea and Deadpool.\n- In 2016, Vincent Cirelli worked at Luma Pictures as a visual effects supervisor on Doctor Strange.\n- At the 89th Academy Awards, Vincent Cirelli received a nomination for the Academy Award for Best Visual Effects for Doctor Strange.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
